# AI Civ training situations v1
# Machine row format: correct_output_slot|candidate_output_slots|nonzero_input_slots|target_output_slots|short_description
# Comment blocks explain the game meaning of each slot used by the following machine row.
# situation 0: action worker case: worker on fresh grass builds irrigation
# Purpose: teach Action engine worker behavior from unit status, terrain, resource, fog, city, and local 9x9 window cues.
# Object ids are not encoded. Output command record 0 applies to the first unit id stored by ai.js for object record 0.
# Action object fields used here: input[0]=unit type, input[1]=unit state, input[7]=has active task, input[8]=immediate action signal, input[9]=current terrain, input[10]=current resource value, input[11]=nearby resource score, input[12]=fresh-water flag, input[13]=city plot score or military usefulness, input[14]=age/pressure, input[15]=nearest friendly city distance.
# Local 9x9 window slots are input[16..96], scanned row-major from map offset di=-4,dj=-4 to di=+4,dj=+4. Slot input[56] is the center tile under this unit. Negative local values such as -0.200000 represent fog-of-war or unknown tiles.
# Forwarded strategy focus fields are relative to this unit: input[97]=target dx, input[98]=target dy, input[99]=military attack priority, input[100]=defense or worker-support priority. dx/dy are normalized by the 9x9 window radius of 4 tiles. Browser runtime fills military focus for military records and worker-support focus for worker records; settlers and explorers keep these fields at zero.
# Cue meaning: center tile is grass with irrigation/fresh-water support.
# Decision meaning: irrigate because grass with fresh water should become a stronger food tile.
# Legal output candidates: output[0] = goto; output[1] = wait; output[3] = road to; output[4] = irrigate; output[5] = chop forest; output[6] = build improvement.
# Correct answer: choose output[4] = irrigate.
# Evaluation rule: after inference, compare only legal candidate outputs; the highest value is the predicted answer.
# Training target: output[4] is set to +0.900000, every other legal candidate output is set to -0.900000.
# input[0] = 0.062500 means unit type normalized as unitTypeIndex/32.
# input[1] = 0.000000 means unit state normalized by the same state order used in ai.js.
# input[7] = 0.000000 means has active task flag; 1.0 means the unit is already busy and should usually preserve its current order.
# input[9] = 0.250000 means current tile terrain type normalized as terrainType/8.
# input[8] = 0.600000 means immediate action signal: workers use 0.80 improvement, 0.60 irrigation, 0.45 chop, 0.30 road, 0.20 road-to; military uses 0.70 adjacent enemy, 0.50 defensive hill.
# input[56] = 0.470000 means main local 9x9 cue driving this action.
# input[99] = 0.000000 means forwarded strategy military attack priority.
# Machine row below repeats the same situation in parser format.
